  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "The bounded target-free translation is not a common-domain repair: it strongly reduces TNG100 Q4, barely changes SIMBA Q4, and worsens Swift Q4 relative to the exact V31 paired donors.",
    "Actual-query alignment beats the shuffled-query control in TNG100 and Swift but not SIMBA, so a domain-common causal alignment rule is not supported.",
    "Descriptor mismatch decreases in every domain while density-tail and field responses do not improve consistently. Minimizing an observation-space translation distance is therefore not equivalent to sampling the conditional density innovation.",
    "The TNG100 response remains evidence that query-residual coupling matters, but the next model must learn a train-only conditional innovation law rather than search over rigid donor translations."
  ],
